Notebook[{
Cell["WolframExample: Rust libraries from the Wolfram Language", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"f9a0facd-edfc-497b-b5c4-58497030c7d7"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook exercises the WolframExample paclet, whose functions are \
implemented in Rust (see WolframExample/Libs). Evaluate it top to bottom.

If the setup section reports a missing paclet, build the library first:
    cd WolframExample && cargo wl build\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a8beb327-f852-45b5-bbda-e82698c19731"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e9e4d3c1-3500-40c1-a4e7-ad6dda022a89"],

Cell["\<\
Both paclets \[LongDash] the hand-written WolframExample and the generated \
WolframExampleLib \[LongDash] sit in this notebook's parent directory, so one \
PacletDirectoryLoad registers both.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3df0cb26-66d7-4cc7-9259-c242e128712c"],

Cell["PacletDirectoryLoad[ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"60bfaf2a-5e1a-406c-98f9-5ecfb8839183"],

Cell["PacletObject[\"WolframExample\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"6f88d58e-558d-4f14-86e2-fc77022e16e0"],

Cell["\<\
The library paclet holds nothing but the compiled dylibs and a generated \
Functions.wl loader:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f98933f0-c9ec-424f-a4f8-824fd91a5dc4"],

Cell["PacletObject[\"WolframExampleLib\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"cd33684b-c4fa-4ad4-b521-cf8ce512ab1e"],

Cell["Needs[\"WolframExample`\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f1d8769a-c9a7-4f08-8d48-2e4096959b45"],

Cell["Everything the package exports:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ef636153-3fae-4e48-a9d3-3d37b881e623"],

Cell["?WolframExample`*", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a3754aab-5152-44c6-adb8-0a1a6f21a3a7"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Math", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e15042ac-4a99-4093-893c-92e4aaa18016"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Scalars and arrays", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"051a075d-d90f-4117-ac2d-9a60003a3166"],

Cell["\<\
A plain Rust function over two f64s. Arguments and result cross as raw \
MArgument scalars \[LongDash] no serialization at all.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"96618bd1-5b59-45ce-b532-b3a297cf8159"],

Cell["ExampleAdd[2, 3]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4c8b9b64-60f4-4a1d-8386-709659c08c41"],

Cell["\<\
NumericArrays are read zero-copy: Rust sees the kernel's own memory, no copy \
and no conversion. Lists are packed into a Real64 NumericArray by the wrapper \
first.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"78883b17-70ff-446c-bf14-2b01a36026e5"],

Cell["ExampleDot[{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"fd9cc0c5-2564-4aa1-b716-a3fb283927e4"],

Cell["\<\
ExampleDot[
    NumericArray[Range[1., 100000.], \"Real64\"],
    NumericArray[Range[100000., 1., -1.], \"Real64\"]
]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"dea09be5-47f4-42a1-a544-dfa57ba14168"],

Cell["\<\
The Rust side accumulates into 8 independent lanes so that LLVM can vectorize \
the loop (see Libs/math/src/lib.rs) \[LongDash] about twice the throughput of \
the naive left-to-right sum. Timed against the kernel's own Dot, which calls \
into BLAS:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e4804338-be21-4ad1-b091-5b4d24fb9e81"],

Cell["\<\
With[{a = Range[1., 100000.], b = Range[100000., 1., -1.]},
    {
        \"Rust\" -> First @ RepeatedTiming @ ExampleDot[a, b],
        \"Kernel\" -> First @ RepeatedTiming @ Dot[a, b]
    }
]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4bbfc85e-6d9a-4974-a321-7ef1d7921c3c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Structs and enums", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"18d7634b-fbe7-4b9f-92ac-9fc7bc5933ad"],

Cell["\<\
Structured arguments cross as WXF. A Rust struct is an Association keyed by \
its field names; the wrapper here presents Wolfram-style capitalized keys.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6f0e2a9d-ca15-4f1b-b8c6-c5cba07dd2ef"],

Cell["ExampleSymmetricPoint[<|\"X\" -> 10, \"Y\" -> 20|>]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"73e09635-493d-4b4b-97d9-88934dc39708"],

Cell["\<\
ExampleArea goes through a Rust enum \[LongDash] one function, one match, two \
shapes:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a85e3945-fbb9-49df-8b3f-7d7fe0e7310b"],

Cell["ExampleArea[<|\"Radius\" -> 1|>]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"98ceb03c-4a27-4ec3-a1d7-9c45b83ccc33"],

Cell["ExampleArea[<|\"Width\" -> 10, \"Height\" -> 20|>]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9b5584d4-238c-4d90-a41d-429c53c24aaa"],

Cell["Table[ExampleArea[<|\"Radius\" -> r|>], {r, 1, 5}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"605c4b14-44e4-429e-8839-308e08f88877"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Errors", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"8c040be1-07a4-4059-932d-11f93f807388"],

Cell["\<\
A Rust Result<f64, String> comes back as {\"Ok\", value} or {\"Err\", \
message}; the wrapper turns the error branch into a Failure.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"677e8bdf-09f3-4337-b21b-267519d96c8f"],

Cell["ExampleSafeDivide[10, 4]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"92b49cad-0e9d-4dea-b80d-4bd798333bc2"],

Cell["ExampleSafeDivide[1, 0]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c6306c3a-3651-442d-ad7a-587805f191e1"],

Cell["So the usual Failure handling applies:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d5a0df2f-2532-44d5-9bfc-7307ed7f7615"],

Cell["\<\
FailureQ /@ {ExampleSafeDivide[1, 2], ExampleSafeDivide[1, 0]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a8ea56d4-d8cd-44e6-aab3-10234653ac4f"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["DuckDB", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ae1d6a8c-b1e5-4f03-a9aa-5483d8ade56f"],

Cell["\<\
An entire embedded SQL engine, statically linked into the library \[LongDash] \
nothing to install. Query results come back as Arrow and are decoded into a \
Tabular.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"39cfd04b-58b6-4399-a5ae-aedc7d73b78d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Scoped connections", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"d9652627-c6f6-4f31-bef1-52d5feb34412"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute opens a connection, applies the function to it, and closes it \
again \[LongDash] even if the body fails.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"479a367c-8a7e-4a7a-b1ee-7a1d2beb7c61"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#, \"SELECT 42 AS answer\"] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"635b9a2b-7bee-4b6b-aecf-6fb2db405925"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT n::INTEGER AS id,
            (n * 1.5)::DOUBLE AS score,
            'item_' || n AS label,
            n % 2 = 0 AS is_even
     FROM generate_series(1, 5) t(n)\"] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f74467cf-086e-440a-8a2e-46b64ec61b11"],

Cell["\<\
The result is an ordinary Tabular, so the usual operations work:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dfad40a4-08af-4d9f-a6e1-31764734047f"],

Cell["\<\
tab = DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT n FROM generate_series(1, 100) t(n)\"] &];
{Length[tab], Total[tab[[All, \"n\"]]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3bffafa5-315c-44fd-9da8-ceb0e03478c8"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Parameters", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b6a39aff-c423-415b-8456-296b294e00a9"],

Cell["\<\
Values are bound to the ? placeholders in order, so nothing is interpolated \
into the SQL string.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"73be5657-51b8-485b-b262-2607f40ce3bd"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT n FROM generate_series(1, 5) t(n) WHERE n > ?\", {2}] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"641f43c7-e740-47f0-bd22-db81c464df55"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT ?::INTEGER + ?::INTEGER AS total\", {20, 22}] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c056339c-7eae-4dac-9df2-d551033c6e04"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Explicit connections", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"2ab6171e-c212-4948-a2b3-7569eee6af51"],

Cell["\<\
For several statements against the same database, hold the handle yourself. \
Here an on-disk file, which persists after disconnecting.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bfc47cd9-52d8-4b5c-852d-b5c760115dc1"],

Cell["\<\
file = FileNameJoin[{$TemporaryDirectory, \"wolfram-example.duckdb\"}];
Quiet[DeleteFile[file]];
conn = DuckDBConnect[\"duckdb:///\" <> file]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9260a7d8-39b7-4832-99d9-2da9122c7709"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBQuery[conn,
    \"CREATE TABLE fruit AS SELECT * FROM (VALUES (1, 'apple'), (2, 'pear')) \
v(id, name)\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9473a0c6-d58e-4b83-87bc-aa9a606aa6d0"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBQuery[conn, \"INSERT INTO fruit VALUES (?, ?)\", {3, \"plum\"}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"35c389a7-1ced-49d7-ac24-a4442a0d86ed"],

Cell["DuckDBQuery[conn, \"SELECT * FROM fruit ORDER BY id\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9031ff69-6159-4eea-a15b-787f253cd7b8"],

Cell["DuckDBDisconnect[conn]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"14ade425-8673-461f-9511-8f225d8990a8"],

Cell["Reopening the same file shows the rows are still there:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b96c40c4-b7f6-4fc5-97cb-41a0e27b4def"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb:///\" <> file,
    DuckDBQuery[#, \"SELECT count(*) AS rows FROM fruit\"] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"41e6344e-023e-4772-aeee-1ad7beab7eaf"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Failures", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"9361446e-5a8a-481a-a7c3-77a3bbd6c424"],

Cell["\<\
Errors from the engine arrive as Failure objects carrying DuckDB's own \
message, and propagate on their own.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"18f0a3af-e43e-4477-9bae-37f947c6c88f"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#, \"SELECT * FROM no_such_table\"] \
&]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a297cacf-3997-4163-8cc7-d486778ea02c"],

Cell["\<\
A handle that has been closed is no longer in the Rust-side registry:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0737ed73-bed1-4891-9722-98f912413852"],

Cell["\<\
With[{c = DuckDBConnect[]},
    DuckDBDisconnect[c];
    DuckDBQuery[c, \"SELECT 1\"]
]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f0d27302-eaf4-436f-9bad-477d17ff75f1"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The raw library", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ba3879a4-84d6-4325-9622-bb565f85a717"],

Cell["\<\
The wrappers in Kernel/WolframExample.wl are a thin layer over an association \
of LibraryFunctions, keyed \"namespace::rust_name\". Anything without a \
wrapper is still one lookup away.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7f843d56-f0ca-48f4-8a3a-a153901cc633"],

Cell["Keys[WolframExampleFunctions[]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4e3e3c0a-fb12-4062-a6ef-db1051e5be42"],

Cell["\<\
inactive_sum builds an expression in Rust and returns it unevaluated:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b86cefbe-5876-4704-a141-a370015a94d4"],

Cell["WolframExampleFunctions[][\"math::inactive_sum\"][{1, 2, 3}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ec9c6f8a-403f-47fa-addf-07cef8ffb726"],

Cell["\<\
Activate[WolframExampleFunctions[][\"math::inactive_sum\"][{1, 2, 3}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"153ab626-57f5-49c1-9c0c-b518fb1c2373"],

Cell["\<\
A panic on the Rust side is caught at the boundary and returned as a Failure \
\[LongDash] it does not take the kernel down:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4d4d31c4-183c-46f1-bb5b-913c240599a0"],

Cell["WolframExampleFunctions[][\"math::panic\"][]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ad8850b3-9b4d-48bb-a79e-d2bc90046709"],

Cell["\<\
And the signatures of everything that was packaged, straight from the \
generated Artifacts.wl asset:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"170d25ba-cfda-4f03-906e-f85dc6293956"],

Cell["\<\
Get[PacletObject[\"WolframExampleLib\"][\"AssetLocation\", \"Artifacts\"]] //
    Map[Query[{\"Name\", \"Signatures\"}]] // Dataset\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7b68650f-ec59-42a7-b196-db90cb9b3120"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Rebuilding", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"16eedd93-0bd5-4b4c-9170-3a8118fc8b49"],

Cell["\<\
After editing the Rust source, rebuild from the paclet directory. The dylibs \
are content-hashed, so a rebuilt library gets a new file name \[LongDash] \
quit the kernel to pick it up.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c27204a9-6ff9-4446-a010-0027e7090675"],

Cell["\<\
ExternalEvaluate[{\"Shell\",
    \"ProcessDirectory\" -> \
FileNameJoin[{ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]], \"WolframExample\"}],
    \"ProcessEnvironment\" -> <|\"PATH\" -> Environment[\"PATH\"]|>},
   \"cargo wl build --release\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"2480edb2-5e06-4e20-8592-af7f0cbaee71"]
}, Open  ]]
},
WindowTitle->"WolframExample Tour",
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (May 6, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"615a22aa-a471-42b3-987f-d8f9fcd59897"
]
